  "findings": [
    "Reference prefill is attention-bound and superlinear: 50.5 -> 145.5 us/token from 8K to 127K (2.9x).",
    "Shooting Brake prefill is transport-bound and nearly flat: 406 -> 494 us/token over the same range (1.2x).",
    "Therefore the prefill gap HALVES with context: 8.0x at 8K -> 3.4x at 127K.",
    "Reference decode ITL grows with KV: 7.02 -> 11.10 ms. Shooting Brake decode is context-independent (fixed 211 us/layer inter-dispatch gap), flat at 11.40 ms.",
    "Therefore decode reaches PARITY at 127K: 11.10 vs 11.40 ms = 1.03x.",
    "Reference concurrency peaks at C=4 and degrades past it; at 96K/127K only C=1-2 admit."
